  "body": "On main `08697d3c4`, the committed program `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.nc` is not the program that the committed project `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` posts.\n\nReading (Windows, debug):\n\n1. Run `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test continuous_4axis_part the_continuous_4axis_part_posts_its_wrapped_program -- --exact` on a clean checkout of main.\n2. The `.camproj` does not change.\n3. The `.nc` changes on 7 lines. Each change is one last digit of an `A` word on a `G0` line at Z0.8746 or Z0.8747. Example: `A-54.14` becomes `A-54.141`, and `A226.344` becomes `A226.345`.\n\nThe test does not see this. Without `WRITE_GOLDEN`, it compares the project text, and it checks only properties of the committed `.nc`. It does not compare the committed `.nc` with a fresh post of the committed project. The guide reader gets a program that differs from the program that the example file posts.\n\nWanted:\n\n- Write the `.nc` again from the committed project. Keep the project as it is. Check that the 7 lines are the only change.\n- Add an assert: the committed project, when loaded, posts the committed `.nc` byte for byte. `first_4axis_part::the_committed_project_posts_the_committed_program` does this for the indexed example.\n\nFound during the clear-out of PR #2554. That PR does not change posted G-code: its branch posts the same 7 lines as main.\n",
